encyclopedia :still_mornings do
  name "Still Mornings"
  summary "Still mornings are the windless resonance calms that settle over a region for a few hours after certain nights — the bands flat, the air carrying sound for extraordinary distances, and every trade that depends on hearing scheduling its finest work into the window."
  kind :phenomenon
  subkind :physical_phenomenon
  status :complete
  topics :resonance, :navigation, :ecology, :music
  prevalence :common
  available_globally
  medium "The local resonance bands and the air itself, region-wide, for a span of hours"
  nature "A morning calm in which band activity drops to seasonal minimum and sound carries far past its ordinary range; loosely forecastable from the tide tables and the night's weather"
  hazard "Sound travels both ways — the calm that lets a listener hear a distant fault lets a distant listener hear everything else"

  descriptive_identity(
    signs: "The morning arrives flat and clear in every register at once: gauges resting, " \
           "gleeds dim, and the first struck bell audible three valleys over, arriving " \
           "small and perfect like something remembered.",
    effects: "Listening work saves itself for the window — span rounds, tasting walks, " \
             "singers' proofs, the long-distance hails between settlements that still " \
             "mornings make briefly possible — and musicians simply get up early.",
    hazards: "The calm carries everything: the fine work and the quarrel, the survey " \
             "hail and the sound of a district's business, three valleys in every " \
             "direction."
  )

  prose <<~PROSE
    Some mornings the world goes flat and clear. A still morning follows certain nights — a deep tide ebb under settled weather, most often, though the almanac offices publish their forecast with more modesty than usual — and for a span of hours the bands rest at their seasonal floor while the air carries sound to extraordinary range: a struck bell audible three valleys over, a dock's morning horn arriving in a settlement that has never seen the dock, conversation from a boat carrying across a full reach of water with every word intact. The calm is region-wide, arrives at dawn, and burns off with the day's first real traffic and heat, and every culture in the system has a name for it that translates, more or less, to the listening hours.

    The trades built their finest work into the window. Span listeners walk their most doubtful stations on still mornings, when the beams speak into silence; the singers prove their choir-true splices; tasters taste; and the settlements that live within a calm's reach of each other keep the old custom of the morning hail — the called exchange between towns, voice to distant voice, that still mornings make possible and tradition has polished into a form: each settlement's caller sends the town's name, its news in a sentence, and its regards, and the answering calls walk back across the distance in the order the sound arrives. The custom is navigation, neighborliness, and census in one breath, and a town whose hail goes unanswered on a clear still morning sends someone to check by road.
  PROSE

  cue "The struck bell arrives from three valleys away, small and perfect, and everyone in the yard pauses in the same breath and says some version of 'still morning' before changing their plans."
  cue "The town's caller stands on the water tower at dawn sending the name, the news, and the regards, and the neighboring towns' answers walk back across the distance in arrival order."
  affordance "The calm is a free instrument upgrade for every listening trade — beams, splices, and tastings read at their truest — and the morning hail custom gives neighboring settlements a working census that costs one caller and one sentence."
  pressure "The air carries everything with equal courtesy, so still mornings are when quarrels, machinery troubles, and private business travel three valleys uninvited — and the settlements' polite fiction of unhearing what the calm delivered is a load-bearing courtesy."
  variation "Valley country hails town to town in long chains; the ring settlements' still mornings run rarer and stranger, hull to hull across vacuum-adjacent silence, and their hail forms are correspondingly brief."
  variation "Musicians treat the windows as the year's true performance slots, and the great still-morning concerts — a single player, audible across a whole region — are announced conditionally and remembered by date."
end
